WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.468
JAKE TAPPER: And our world
lead, a vital remaining

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:05.438
clue into the origins of
the coronavirus pandemic.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.841
But we may never learn
the truth about it.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.876
I'm talking about blood
samples, thousands of them,

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.980
thousands of them sitting in
a Wuhan hospital in China.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.382
After two years, the Chinese
government is preparing

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.583
to test these samples.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.719
But as it stands, the
World Health Organization

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.553
and other foreign
experts will not

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.257
be allowed to analyze
the data independently,

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.391
meaning the Chinese
government is

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.426
in charge of
examining the results

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.694
and revealing their findings.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.398
And as Nick Paton Walsh
reports, the Chinese government

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:34.134
doesn't exactly have a track
record of transparency.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.806
- Ground zero for the illness
sparking global unease.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:44.610
- It is likely a brand
new viral pneumonia.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:47.346
NICK PATON WALSH: It is perhaps
the last publicly known clue

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.883
to where coronavirus came from.

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:53.819
But will the world ever learn
the truth of what it says?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.390
Tens of thousands of tiny
blood samples taken in Wuhan

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:01.361
in the last months of 2019
are still stored in a hospital

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.494
there.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.064
- The samples from the
blood bank absolutely

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.966
will contain vital clues.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.370
- They could potentially
be very revelatory.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.405
- This is the closest
to the world we've

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:16.709
seen of real time samples.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.245
NICK PATON WALSH: The samples
might reveal when and even

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.613
where antibodies
against the virus

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.483
first appeared in humans
in October or November

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.519
two years ago.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:29.622
China says they had to be
kept for legal reasons for two

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:33.426
years in case of lawsuits
over the blood transfusions

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.695
they are from.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.764
But now, that limit is
almost up for the key months

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.433
at the end of 2019.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.502
And a Chinese official
confirmed to CNN

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.605
that China is
preparing to test them,

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:49.008
echoing a promise from
July when they said

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.877
they would share the results.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:54.246 line:14%
- [non-english speech]

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.515 line:8%
NICK PATON WALSH:
Related institutions

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.817 line:8%
from the Chinese
side, he says, also

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.352 line:8%
express that once
they have the results,

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.723 line:8%
they will deliver them to both
the Chinese and foreign expert

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:04.924 line:14%
teams.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:07.026
The samples come from
the disposable tubes that

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.695
carried donor blood
into the donor bag

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:13.499
and are something the WHO
team said earlier this year

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.867
they wanted to examine.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.169
- Team for the origins
of the coronavirus.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.371
NICK PATON WALSH:
They could contain

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.673
vital detailed information.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:26.245 line:8%
- Might also help us to follow
the trajectory of the spread

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:29.816 line:8%
of the virus by
tracking the individuals

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.951 line:14%
who may carry the virus.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.787
- And you would like to go
back to find out exactly

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:39.358
during which month
this virus started

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:43.562
to leave fingerprints in the
human population in China.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.999
- It is common practice to
de-identify the samples.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.337
So you could strip it down
to basic demographics, age,

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:54.006
gender, neighborhood,
where they lived.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.575
All of those data
will be available.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.444
NICK PATON WALSH: But the
same problem emerges again.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:01.314
It will be China and China
alone doing the testing

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:02.815
and reporting their results.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:06.118
The US's recent report into
the origins of the coronavirus

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.988
and statements from allies
have all demanded greater

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.690
transparency from China.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.226
But now, this key
data is being examined

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.094
a full two years later.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:19.232
And there's no plan as it stands
for outsiders like the WHO

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.667
to be allowed in on it.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:24.570
- In order to make it convincing
and credible, the results,

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:30.409
I mean, ideally,
you want to involve

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.513
the WHO or the foreign experts.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.716
- I'm not completely
certain that China

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:40.620
has not done this testing and
has not shared the results.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:43.789
- What we always say
is trust but verify.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:48.994
It surely would be better if the
Chinese scientists would permit

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:53.366
external scientists to be
with them to collaborate

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.201
to do this all together.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.770
NICK PATON WALSH: But
instead, this vital remaining

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:01.774
clue risks being mired in
recriminations and uncertainty

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:02.675
again.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.780
Two years, Jake.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.183
Still two years now since
the virus most likely,

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:14.353
according to a lot of the
studies, got into humans.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.021
We're still asking
these questions.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.591
It's not like China
isn't extremely curious,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.493
doesn't spend millions every
year in trying to learn

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.229
more about viruses in general.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.364
So you heard one of the
experts touch on it there.

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:28.601
There is some skepticism as
to whether these tests may not

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.769
possibly have already been done.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.472
But great pressure for them
to happen possibly again,

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.942
or for the first time now
and for those results,

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:38.477
if not even the process
to be made public

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.278
and shared globally.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.679
Jake.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.181
JAKE TAPPER: Nick, where does
this leave the ongoing debate

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:44.583
about the origins of COVID?

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:45.884
NICK PATON WALSH:
Yeah, I mean, look.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.187
This has been a huge issue
of geopolitical contention.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.957
China's rivals pointing at it
essentially saying that maybe

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:51.991
a lab leak was involved.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.160
The evidence behind
that not public.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.428
And so this particular
set of samples

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.364
could, if they
revealed a cluster

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:01.033
around people near a
laboratory, point to that.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:03.602
But more likely, it's all
about leading to where

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.871
the natural origins of
this could have been,

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.074
the Southern supply
chains of wet markets,

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:11.110
other places in China
which are known areas where

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.846
the viruses could have spread
into humans in the past,

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.414
and trying to dig into that.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.883
That's what this is such a
vital set of live clues for.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.118
Jake.
JAKE TAPPER: All right, Nick.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:19.918
Thanks so much.

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.019
Appreciate it.

